# Local Laya server runtime: pid file, stdout/stderr logs, and the `--dump-states` corpus.
# tools/laya-ctl.ps1 writes these next to itself, which is the repo root when the repo's copy is used.
# The dumps are the raw requests a match sent (2000+ files and growing) -- inputs to analysis, not sources.
.laya-server.pid
.laya-server.out.log
.laya-server.err.log
.laya-states/
.laya-venv/

